SDL2: a gamepad with buttons and no axes is a joystick

SDL_EVDEV_GuessDeviceClass, as udev's input_id, counts a device as a
joystick only beside an X and a Y axis. The TrimUI Brick's buttons, its
d-pad among them, are keys alone (plastron's brick-pad), so SDL saw no
joystick, and a port's gptokeyb - which turns the pad into keys - had
nothing to read. This counts the face buttons (BTN_GAMEPAD) with a d-pad
or a Start button as a joystick too.

ChaOS, for ports only (src/ports.h). After plastron's 0001 and 0002.

diff --git a/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c b/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c
index 472cc2f..2823fd2 100644
--- a/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c
+++ b/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c
@@ -104,6 +104,16 @@ SDL_EVDEV_GuessDeviceClass(const unsigned long bitmask_ev[NBITS(EV_MAX)],
         }
     }
 
+    /* ChaOS: a gamepad with buttons alone, its d-pad included, and no axes
+     * at all - the TrimUI Brick's, as plastron's kernel has it - is a
+     * joystick too. udev's input_id says so of the face buttons
+     * (BTN_GAMEPAD), but only looks for them beside axes. */
+    if (!(devclass & SDL_UDEV_DEVICE_JOYSTICK) && test_bit(EV_KEY, bitmask_ev) &&
+        test_bit(BTN_GAMEPAD, bitmask_key) &&
+        (test_bit(BTN_DPAD_UP, bitmask_key) || test_bit(BTN_START, bitmask_key))) {
+        devclass |= SDL_UDEV_DEVICE_JOYSTICK;
+    }
+
     if (test_bit(EV_REL, bitmask_ev) &&
         test_bit(REL_X, bitmask_rel) && test_bit(REL_Y, bitmask_rel) &&
         test_bit(BTN_MOUSE, bitmask_key)) {
